      "id": "isthmus_observer_deposit_vault_timing",
      "comment": "Two txs in one block: tx0 is a plain EIP-1559 transfer whose own fee settlement credits coinbase/BaseFeeVault/L1FeeVault/OperatorFeeVault; tx1 is a deposit tx to the observer contract, reading those same four vaults' BALANCE *after* tx0 has committed. Unlike isthmus_observer_normal_basic (same-tx timing: vault reads happen before that tx's own settlement), this vector checks *cross-tx* visibility: tx1 should see tx0's credited amounts layered on top of the tiny pre-block markers (1/2/3/4), proving vault credits from an earlier tx in the same block are visible to a later tx's execution (ordinary state persistence, but worth a dedicated machine check given this is exactly the class of timing bug spec Section 4.3 warns about).",
